## Our changes relative to upstream

All changes are ours; no third-party material beyond the upstream above was adapted.
The upstream's own NOTICE/attribution remains intact in its `LICENSE`.

| Area | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/server.ts` | Tool surface narrowed/restructured (net −582 / +251 lines across the tree). Upstream registered **37** tools (`registerTool(` count at upstream `8311c9a`); the live surface is **30** after merging upstream `eb05ae9`. |
| `src/tools/bannerlord-editor.ts`, `src/utils/bannerlord-editor-client.ts`, `src/utils/bannerlord-editor-client.test.ts`, `tools/editor-probe/` | Merged from upstream `eb05ae9` (experimental local editor MCP preview). `bannerlord_editor_status` lives in the query-first tier; the five action tools live in the authoring (`full`) tier, matching this variant's tiering. |
| `src/utils/bannerlord-editor-registry.test.ts` | Adapted from upstream `eb05ae9`: hard-coded upstream tool counts (36/43) replaced with this variant's counts (23/30), so the registry test validates this variant's actual registration. |
| `src/utils/bannerlord-toolset.ts` | Toolset mode resolution adjusted; editor tool names added to the tier lists. |
| `knowledge/`, `src/utils/own-docs.ts`, `src/scripts/index-own-docs.ts`, `src/utils/docs-db.ts` | New **own knowledge base**: default docs source is our in-repo `knowledge/` corpus (own modding references + MCP suite docs), section-split and FTS-indexed. External web docs are opt-in. |
| `src/tools/search-docs.ts`, `src/tools/search-knowledge.ts`, `src/tools/bannerlord-index-status.ts`, `src/scripts/setup.ts` | Own knowledge layer wired in as the default docs source; external official/community docs downgraded to opt-in. |
| `src/utils/bannerlord-module-tooling.ts` | **Fixed a symlink blind spot**: `walkFiles()` used `entry.isFile()` only, which is `false` for symbolic links. With mod managers that install via symlinks (e.g. Vortex), every `Modules/<mod>/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/*.dll` was invisible, so `bannerlord_doctor` reported **39 false `missing_declared_submodule_dll` warnings** (verified 39/39 false positives). Fixed by following links and classifying the target (directory → recurse, file → yield, broken link → skip). Measured effect on this machine: DLLs found went from 1 to 130 across a 6-module sample; doctor issues went from 41 to 2. |
| `src/utils/bannerlord-setup.ts` | Same symlink fix (byte-identical `walkFiles` helper). |
| `src/utils/game-profiles.ts` | Same symlink fix (byte-identical `walkFiles` helper). |
| `src/tools/get-entity.ts` | New tool. |
| `src/tools/project-memory-rw.ts` | New tool. |
| `src/tools/bannerlord-index-status.ts`, `src/scripts/verify-bannerlord.ts` | Minor adjustments. |
| `README.md`, `README_zh.md` | Rewritten sections. |

> The three `walkFiles` helpers were byte-identical before the fix; the same defect
> existed in three places and was fixed in all three.

## Runtime dependencies

Unchanged in kind from upstream: the server runs on Bun and consumes the project's own
dependencies. No new runtime dependency was introduced by this variant.

